    "rule": "a row is exactly {session, resume, state}: session 32 lowercase hex, resume 64 lowercase hex (SHA-256 of the resume token), state exactly {overrides, locks, formsLeft}, or those and unanswered (the distinct kinds the session has left one form unanswered of: none of them locked, and only with a form spent, formsLeft under 3); overrides at most 64, one per name, each exactly {name, value, loosening, over, version}: a cap has an integer value within the settings tool's bounds (maxOutputBytes 1048576 to 268435456, requestTimeout 5000 to 120000), version null, and over a positive integer when loosening is true, else null; pack.<n> (^pack\\.[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,63}$) has a boolean value, over null and a semver version (required, never null); locks distinct kinds of maxOutputBytes, requestTimeout, pack, module (every module.<package>.<setting> is the one kind module); formsLeft an integer 0 to 3; at most 64 KiB as JSON. The restore message is exactly {id, type: \"restore\", sessions, declines, reset}: reset lists the sessions (each a row's) that lost loosenings in a handoff, to be told so",
